--
libstdc++ 13 <algorithm>: std::ranges::copy(first, last, out) is a
conversion error ("file bits/ranges_algobase.h line 311: found no match for
symbol 'operator()'"); with a range argument the body of __copy_fn's range
overload (ranges_algobase.h:311) is dropped instead, and the copy is
nondeterministic.  The same drop shows when <format> or <chrono> is
included.  Being reduced; a header-free imitation of __copy_fn passes.
Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 accepts this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
